Architecture plan for issues #100 and #101

Project shape
- Existing Next.js App Router application with public article rendering in app/(public)/blog/[slug]/page.tsx.
- Article page currently owns the Markdown renderer, signed image URL resolution, JSON-LD metadata, and author aside markup.
- No backend/schema changes are required for these two issues.

Module structure and file organization
- Keep both changes localized to app/(public)/blog/[slug]/page.tsx unless the component grows enough to justify extraction.
- Add a small MyClawTeamCard presentational component near the existing article-page helpers/components and render it immediately after ReactMarkdown and before the author aside.
- Add a LinkifiedText helper in the same file to render text segments from post.authorIntro. It should split only URL substrings and preserve surrounding plain text without changing stored data.

Dependencies between issues
- #100 inserts a new card in the article content flow before the author card.
- #101 changes the rendering inside the existing author card. It is independent of #100 except both touch the same article page file, so implement in separate branches and rebase/pull main between issues to avoid conflicts.

Key design decisions
- Use semantic, accessible markup and existing editorial styling tokens for the new about card.
- LinkifiedText should render external URLs with target="_blank" and rel="noreferrer" and use the editorial red link treatment consistent with Markdown links.
- Avoid schema, database, auth, email, storage, and routing changes.
- Do not introduce new dependencies; URL detection can be handled with a small regex and React node composition.
